      "title": "Mock 2 — Highlight Incorrect Words Q1 (Ending poverty)",
      "category": "mock-2",
      "audioText": "For some people, this proposition may seem far fetched, but ending poverty is both morally necessary and actually feasible. All of us must play a role in making it happen. All human beings want, and have a right to live in dignity, to determine our own destinies, and to be respected by other, by other people. Despite the universality of these rights, our capacities to fulfill them vary enormously, and no dividing line is more profound in influencing the quality of our lives than the gulf between poverty and prosperity.",
